NAME
       netstat - show network connections and listening ports (old tool)

SYNOPSIS
       netstat [-t] [-u] [-l] [-n] [-p]

DESCRIPTION
       netstat lists network sockets. It is part of the net-tools package,
       which RHEL 9 no longer installs by default: use ss, which takes the
       same main options and prints the same kind of table. Both show which
       program listens on which port, which is how you check that a service
       really listens where you configured it.

OPTIONS
       -t     TCP sockets.

       -u     UDP sockets.

       -l     Only listening sockets.

       -n     Show numbers instead of names for addresses and ports.

       -p     Show the program and PID that owns each socket (root sees all).

EXAMPLES
           ss -tlnp
           netstat -tlnp      (after dnf install net-tools)

SEE ALSO
       ss(8), ip(8), firewall-cmd(1)
